<h1><hr class="Journal2">TRAVEL WRITING DAY - Friday, August 20, 2004<hr class="Journal2"></h1>
<p>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Mishaps/20040820_1.JPG&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Mishaps/20040820_1_sm.JPG"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20040820/P1010009.JPG&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20040820/Small/P1010009.JPG"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20040820/P1010011.JPG&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20040820/Small/P1010011.JPG"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20040820/P1010018.JPG&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20040820/Small/P1010018.JPG"></a>
<p>
Spend the entire day travel writing.  In the evening I have a run-in with one of the residents living near where I've been van camping.  After setting the homeowner straight on my intentions (mission, website, etc), he walks away and I think everything has been taken care of.  Yeah, right...
<p>
To steer clear of any more unpleasant encounters I leave the neighborhood.  On my way to a nearby car wash I... WHAM!!!  I get busted by the cops!  Seems the paranoid resident ratted me out, even after I talked to the dude and gave him my travel business card.  Some people are just overly paranoid I guess, not much I can do about that.  However, looking on the bright side, the van ends the day squeaky clean as I ready it for more road traveling adventure.
<p>
